# Shell scripts must stay LF even when checked out on Windows: a CRLF in a .sh breaks the shebang and every
# command when the file runs on the Linux CI runner (\r is treated as part of the interpreter path / args).
*.sh text eol=lf

# The shared rg-command case table (bench/golden/ap6/rg-command-cases.tsv) is replayed through a bash
# script and through a C# theory; a CRLF would put a stray CR into every expected verdict.
*.tsv text eol=lf
